ok 20 - lineage: a row never supersedes itself [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 21 - lineage: the audience follows ^[a-z0-9_-]{1,48}$ (E4) [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 22 - lineage: the audience is at most 48 characters [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 23 - lineage: the settings snapshot ordinal is positive [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 24 - lineage: a revision of another entry cannot be published under this entry [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 25 - lineage: the owner is the entry owner, never another party [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 26 - lineage: control - the fixture hash equals the SHA-256 of the hand-written canonical JSON (sorted keys, null predecessor) [P2-S11-AC-116]
ok 27 - lineage: the stored publication hash is recomputed from the row [P2-S11-AC-116]
ok 28 - lineage: the lineage id of a first row is its own id [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 29 - lineage: the lineage locale is the revision locale [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 30 - lineage: a lineage cannot begin with a tombstone [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 31 - lineage: the author of the revision never publishes it (E11) [P2-S11-AC-107]
ok 32 - lineage: only an approved review with the same dependency hash can be published [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 33 - lineage: a publish row is not appended for an entry that is no longer active [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 34 - lineage: the first publish row opens the lineage at version 1 [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 35 - lineage: a second lineage for the same entry, locale and audience is refused by the lineage key [P2-S11-AC-115]
ok 36 - lineage: another audience is another lineage [P2-S11-AC-115]
ok 37 - lineage: a successor continues the sequence with the previous version + 1 [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 38 - lineage: a successor stays in the lineage of its predecessor [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 39 - lineage: a tombstone copies the ended row's revision and evidence [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 40 - lineage: a tombstone copies the settings ordinal too [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 41 - lineage: an unpublish of the active head appends one revoked tombstone [P2-S11-AC-115]
ok 42 - lineage: expiry, archive and unpublish need an active head [P2-S11-AC-115]
ok 43 - lineage: a successor of a row that is no longer the head loses with publication_conflict [P2-S11-AC-115]
ok 44 - lineage: a revoked lineage is published again with a new head row [P2-S11-AC-115]
ok 45 - lineage: the members lineage opens at version 1 [P2-S11-AC-115]
