ok 13 - the platform_api wrapper is executable by service_role only, not by PUBLIC, anon or authenticated [P2-S11-AC-081]
ok 14 - an unknown key, a missing member, a malformed id or version and a non-object proof are INVALID_REQUEST, an absent schedule is NOT_FOUND, and none of them changed a durable table (observed inside each call before it rolled back) [P2-S11-AC-079]
ok 15 - a stale lease, a stale version and a schedule that was never claimed are refused (CONFLICT / VERSION_MISMATCH) and none of them changed a durable table (observed inside each call before it rolled back) [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 16 - a claimed, due publish schedule executes [P2-S11-AC-080]
ok 17 - the answer is exactly the six-member ScheduleExecutionResult [P2-S11-AC-079]
ok 18 - the result names the appended lineage row, the actual instant and the deviation from the resolved instant (about a minute late here) [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 19 - the schedule is completed at version 3 with actual_at_utc and deviation_seconds = round(actual - resolved), its lease released [P2-S11-AC-084]
ok 20 - the lineage head carries the schedule id, the schedule creator as publisher and the frozen evidence and version set [P2-S11-AC-084]
ok 21 - exactly one identifier-only cms.publication.changed.v1 and one system audit record (the claim's correlation, no actor) commit with the schedule; the revision is published [P2-S11-AC-084]
ok 22 - the result carries no publisher, author, party or review identifier [P2-S11-AC-081]
ok 23 - a repeated execution of a completed schedule answers already_completed with the original lineage row, instant and deviation and adds no lineage row, event or audit record [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 24 - unpublish, expire and archive schedules complete [P2-S11-AC-084]
ok 25 - each tombstone is a revoked successor row at version 2 that names the ended head and the schedule and copies its revision and evidence, with revoked_at set and no activation [P2-S11-AC-114]
ok 26 - each tombstone emitted exactly one cms.publication.changed.v1 at lineage version 2 [P2-S11-AC-116]
ok 27 - an unpublish without an active head blocks the schedule with publication_not_active and appends nothing [P2-S11-AC-083]
ok 28 - a schedule that fell due two hours ago still executes and records a deviation of about 7,200 seconds [P2-S11-AC-083]
