ok 25 - with a template the instances follow its slot order (primary) and an instance in an unknown slot comes last [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 26 - the workflow_read phase is the submit phase: the same document for the same revision [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 27 - the schedule and publish phases bind to the approved review's FROZEN dependency hash (NOT_FOUND when there is no approved review) and need no manifest build; the submit phase of a revision whose manifest cannot be built (an unregistered block) is DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 28 - the schedule and publish phases load the same document; a block key/version missing from the registry reports unregistered with the digest the instance recorded [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 29 - the execute phase loads the schedule's revision for the sweep with no session, bound to the hash it was given [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 30 - a hash other than the schedule's frozen one, an absent schedule and a revision that is not the schedule's are NOT_FOUND; a context member on the service shape is INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 31 - an owner-party publisher and a reviewer assignee of a review of the revision hold the read scope [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 32 - a member with no scope, an unassigned reviewer, a non-member, an absent entry, a revision of another entry, an archived entry and another acting party are ONE indistinguishable NOT_FOUND [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 33 - a held entry loads; a revision id alone resolves its entry; neither an entry nor a revision is INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 34 - an unknown phase, a missing phase or context, an unknown member and a malformed id are INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 35 - a document above 1 MiB is the uniform NOT_FOUND (the Worker then sends no evidence) [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok 36 - the load writes nothing: no audit record, event, reservation, review, schedule or publication is created or changed [P2-S11-AC-101]
ok
